# Test: a live edit of service { geodns } reaches the geodns plugin
# Initial config: geodns serves zone a.example.
# After SIGHUP:   geodns serves a.example. and b.example.
# Expected: geodns installs the reloaded config at apply and logs it with
#           both zones counted.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-plugin-reload-applies-or-refuses row 23, AC-1: geodns's
#            verify/apply pair publishes the resolver snapshot of the reloaded
#            config (geodnsInstaller.install).
# PREVENTS: the acked-and-dropped reload. With OnConfigure alone, the SDK
#           answers config-apply OK and calls nothing, so the commit succeeded
#           while geodns kept answering from the boot zones until a restart.
#
# DISCRIMINATION: the "zones=2" line is written only by install, which only
# the apply handler calls on a reload. Without the handler the expectation
# fails. That an edit elsewhere under service publishes nothing is proven in
# Go by TestConfigTxUnchangedSubtreeIsNoop (geodns/config_tx_unchanged_test.go).

option=env:var=ze.log.geodns:value=info

stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
service {
	geodns {
		enabled false
		zone a.example.
		nameserver 192.0.2.53
	}
}
EOF_CONF

tmpfs=config2.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF2
service {
	geodns {
		enabled false
		zone a.example.
		zone b.example.
		nameserver 192.0.2.53
	}
}
EOF_CONF2

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=le test fixture reload/tx-protocol-sighup-trigger
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp:timeout=20s
await=stderr:contains=sighup reload complete:then=stop
expect=stderr:pattern=geodns: config applied.*zones=1
expect=stderr:pattern=geodns: config applied.*zones=2
reject=stderr:contains=reload error
reject=stderr:pattern=panic
